# sqllogictest scripts, run by //src/test/scala/com/transformer/slt:slt_test.
# sqlite/ holds files of SQLite's corpus (https://www.sqlite.org/sqllogictest,
# free to copy as its COPYRIGHT says); postgres/ ports of PostgreSQL's
# regression tests, with Postgres's answers, under the PostgreSQL License
# (postgres/COPYRIGHT), and in postgres/sql/ and postgres/expected/ each ported
# file's source and the output psql printed for it, which slt_test checks the
# ports' answers against; spark/ ports of Spark's SQLQueryTestSuite files, with
# Spark's ANSI answers, written by //src/test/scala/com/transformer/slt:spark_import,
# under the Apache License 2.0 (spark/LICENSE and spark/NOTICE); cockroach/
# files of CockroachDB's logic tests at v23.2.0, vendored with the condition
# lines that say what the engine does with each record, under the Apache License
# 2.0 since their BSL's Change Date, 2026-10-01 (cockroach/LICENSE,
# cockroach/NOTICE; postgresjoin.test also under the PostgreSQL License,
# cockroach/POSTGRESQL-LICENSE); datafusion/ files of Apache DataFusion's
# sqllogictest files at 934691e, vendored the same way, and in datafusion/data/
# the CSV files they read, under the Apache License 2.0 (datafusion/LICENSE,
# datafusion/NOTICE); tpch/ TPC-H's queries over RisingWave's tiny TPC-H tables
# with RisingWave's answers, its CREATE TABLE and INSERT files included as they
# are (tpch/LICENSE, tpch/NOTICE); agreed/ queries the fuzz generators drew with
# the answers PostgreSQL and DuckDB agree on, written by
# //src/test/scala/com/transformer/slt:agreed_corpus (plans/testing/14), each
# script's header naming its seeds, the tool's commit and both references'
# versions; every other script is this repo's own. A `.data` file
# is a table's rows, which a script loads with COPY: postgres/data/ holds
# Postgres's own, as its regression suite loads them.
filegroup(
    name = "scripts",
    srcs = glob([
        "**/*.test",
        "**/*.data",
        "datafusion/data/*.csv",
        "tpch/*.slt.part",
        "postgres/sql/*.sql",
        "postgres/expected/*.out",
    ]),
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
